      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril works by directly inhibiting the angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE), which blocks the conversion of angiotensin I into angiotensin II. Since angiotensin II is the primary driver of vasoconstriction and aldosterone release in the RAAS, its reduction leads to dilated blood vessels and decreased sodium retention. This sequence effectively lowers blood pressure by relaxing the arterial smooth muscle and reducing the workload on your heart.",
